      "writtenOn": "2023-11-13T23:35:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The goal of this edit was to make sure the script doesn\u0027t spam error messages for a single missing policy that covers multiple states, because the `led-policy` binding allows for states to be unspecified for \"match any\".\n\nFor Example, in the old patchset, if a board has a policy that only specifies the `chipset-state` but ignores all the other factors, and only covered S0 and S3 but missed S5, the error message generated would be:\n```\nNo LED policy found for LED_PWRS_CHARGE, port 0, POWER_S5.\nNo LED policy found for LED_PWRS_CHARGE, port 1, POWER_S5.\nNo LED policy found for LED_PWRS_DISCHARGE, port 0, POWER_S5.\nNo LED policy found for LED_PWRS_DISCHARGE, port 1, POWER_S5.\nNo LED policy found for LED_PWRS_ERROR, port 0, POWER_S5.\nNo LED policy found for LED_PWRS_ERROR, port 1, POWER_S5.\nNo LED policy found for LED_PWRS_FORCED_IDLE, port 0, POWER_S5.\nNo LED policy found for LED_PWRS_FORCED_IDLE, port 1, POWER_S5.\nNo LED policy found for LED_PWRS_CHARGE_NEAR_FULL, port 0, POWER_S5.\nNo LED policy found for LED_PWRS_CHARGE_NEAR_FULL, port 1, POWER_S5.\n```\n\nWith the new patchset, the error message will just be \n```\nNo LED policy found for POWER_S5.\n```",
      "parentUuid": "d0130ef4_a1d25d5e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "fcd86a4fdbec68f2964b8fb8184b35dc86b19df3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
